{
 "_comment": [
  "THE single source of truth for stations: coordinates, time zones, slugs,",
  "and the codes each source knows them by. Read by src/lib/locations.ts and",
  "by fetch/ in Python.",
  "",
  "It exists because these rows used to live in both languages. They drifted,",
  "and the drift was invisible: fetch/cams.py keyed three Australian stations",
  "au-eme, au-gld and au-hob while ARPANSA calls them emd, gco and kin, so",
  "those forecasts could never join the cities they belonged to.",
  "",
  "Coordinates are the INSTRUMENT's position where one exists, not the city",
  "centre: ARPANSA's Sydney station is 20 km south of the CBD, and a CAMS",
  "grid cell is about 44 km across."
 ],
